  "details": "I hope to enable avatars to retrieve textures via VideoPlayer. \n\nThis would go beyond simply carrying a portable player; it could provide features like dynamic backgrounds or animated textures to create various clever effects. \n\nHowever, it may be necessary to limit the resolution for each avatar. This is because hardware decoders require a larger buffer to fully utilize the hardware. \n\nFurthermore, while the performance gap in hardware decoders is much smaller than that of 3D performance, there are still significant differences between different GPU models and generations.\n\nCurrent widespread compatibility generally limits us to H.264. \n\nHowever, providing this feature would allow players to reduce download sizes while achieving sufficient dynamic texture effects. \n\nThe trade-off is merely utilizing the hardware decoder, which often sits idle and may only impact performance by about 3%. \n\nOn the other hand, this could lead to massive VRAM overhead, potentially making it as demanding as—or even heavier than—real-time lighting. \n\nThis necessitates limits on the active resolution or the number of concurrent streams per user. \n\nExisting methods result in enormous download sizes and much lower quality; textures cannot remain clear enough without exceeding storage limits. \n\nThis implementation would also allow for long-duration periodic changes.",
